-- title:
--   Base change injectivity for differentials of q-expansion function fields
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, $K$ a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure, and $\Gamma \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ a subgroup of finite index with $T \in \Gamma$. For a field $L$, write $F_L =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC L Γ` for the intermediate field of $L((q))$ over $L$ generated by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,L\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,L\,p_g$, where $f, g$ range over modular forms of a common weight $k$ on the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$, $p_f, p_g$ are integral power series satisfying `IsIntegralQExp` for $f$ and $g$ respectively, and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,L\,p_g \neq 0$. The assertion is that there is a $K$-linear map $\Phi : K \otimes_k \Omega_{F_k/k} \to \Omega_{F_K/K}$ which is injective and which satisfies the following compatibility: for all $c \in K$, all $f, g \in F_k$ and all $f', g' \in F_K$ whose underlying Laurent series are the coefficientwise images of those of $f$ and $g$ under $\mathrm{algebraMap}\;k\;K$, one has $\Phi(c \otimes (f \cdot \mathrm{d}g)) = c \cdot (f' \cdot \mathrm{d}g')$, the differentials being taken in $\Omega_{F_k/k}$ and $\Omega_{F_K/K}$ respectively.
--
--   This is the base-change step for Kähler differentials of the $q$-expansion function field of $X(\Gamma)$: the $K$-span of the differentials already defined over $k$ is identified with $K \otimes_k \Omega_{F_k/k}$, the map being in general not surjective when $K/k$ is transcendental. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_linearMap_injective_tensorProduct_kaehler_map_ssPolarDifferentials_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_linearMap_injective_tensorProduct_kaehler_map_ssPolarDifferentials_eq), and rests on the injectivity of the $q$-expansion map on differentials, [`ModularCurve.diffQExp_qExpFunctionFieldC_injective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.diffQExp_qExpFunctionFieldC_injective).
-- source:
